.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SYSCTL 3
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysctl ,
.Nm sysctlbyname ,
.Nm sysctlnametomib
.Nd get or set kernel state
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sysctl.h
.Ft int
.Fo sysctl
.Fa "const int *name"
.Fa "unsigned int namelen"
.Fa "void *oldp"
.Fa "size_t *oldlenp"
.Fa "const void *newp"
.Fa "size_t newlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo sysctlbyname
.Fa "const char *name"
.Fa "void *oldp"
.Fa "size_t *oldlenp"
.Fa "const void *newp"
.Fa "size_t newlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlnametomib "const char *name" "int *mibp" "size_t *sizep"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The kernel keeps a tree of named, typed variables, its management
information base.
Every variable has a numeric name, an array of integers such as
.Brq Dv CTL_KERN , KERN_OSTYPE ,
and a dotted text name such as
.Va kern.ostype .
.Pp
The
.Fn sysctl
function reads the variable named by the
.Fa namelen
integers at
.Fa name ,
of which there are at least 2 and at most
.Dv CTL_MAXNAME .
If
.Fa oldp
is not
.Dv NULL ,
the value is copied there and
.Fa *oldlenp ,
which gave the room available, is set to the number of bytes copied.
If
.Fa oldp
is
.Dv NULL
and
.Fa oldlenp
is not, only the size of the value is stored at
.Fa *oldlenp .
If
.Fa newp
is not
.Dv NULL ,
the variable is then set to the
.Fa newlen
bytes there.
.Pp
The
.Fn sysctlbyname
function does the same for a variable given by its text name, and
.Fn sysctlnametomib
converts a text name to a numeric one, storing at most
.Fa *sizep
integers at
.Fa mibp
and their number at
.Fa *sizep .
.Pp
Numbers below 256 are fixed, and the
.Dv CTL_* ,
.Dv KERN_* ,
.Dv VM_*
and
.Dv HW_*
constants in
.In sys/sysctl.h
name them; other variables are numbered when the kernel registers them, and
programs must look them up by text name.
.Pp
The node numbered 0 describes the tree.
.Brq 0 , 1 , Ar oid
returns the text name of
.Ar oid ;
.Brq 0 , 2 , Ar oid
returns the numeric name of the variable after it, in depth-first order,
passing over variables flagged
.Dv CTLFLAG_SKIP ;
.Brq 0 , 3
converts the text name given as new data to a numeric name;
.Brq 0 , 4 , Ar oid
returns its type and flags as an
.Vt unsigned int ,
followed by its format string; and
.Brq 0 , 5 , Ar oid
returns its description.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa namelen
is less than 2 or more than
.Dv CTL_MAXNAME ,
or a new value has the wrong size.
.It Bq Er EISDIR
The name is a node, not a variable.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
Nothing has that name.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The value is longer than
.Fa *oldlenp ;
as much as fits has been copied.
.It Bq Er EPERM
A new value was given by a user other than the superuser, or for a variable
that is read-only or a tunable.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn sysctl
function first appeared in
.Bx 4.4 .
OxideBSD's follows the interface of
.Fx ,
whose numbering it uses.
